| `launcher` | Decides where a long script runs on a shared host, here, here at a lower CPU priority, or on a farm through a config adapter, prints the reasons on one line, starts the command from the allowlisted environment and records how long it took. | `python3 scripts/launch.py -- make verify` | [`launcher.farm.adapter`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Defence in depth, not a scheduler: no queue, no retry, no CPU or memory cap; the shipped farm adapter is `none`. | [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
